~ start
Rowan: Bridge is holding. That's a good day by my standards.
- What are you working on?
	Rowan: Mostly the east rail today. Water finds every weak joint eventually.
	=> start
- Any advice for the mine?
	Rowan: Take a pickaxe, keep your energy up, and don't let the quiet fool you. Old places make their own trouble.
	=> start
- See you later.
	Rowan: Keep your tools dry.
	=> END

~ friend_2
Rowan: You have stopped looking like someone borrowing tools and started looking like someone who knows why they break.
- I will take that as a compliment.

Rowan: You should. I do not hand them out often.

=> END

~ friend_4
Rowan: If you ever need a hand reinforcing the farm, ask before the roof is already falling in.
- I thought you liked difficult repairs.

Rowan: I like repairs. I dislike preventable ones.

=> END

~ heart_2
Rowan: Hold this end of the rail for me.
Rowan: Most people only notice a bridge when it fails. You have been showing up before things fail.
Rowan: That matters more than people think.
- Reliable work deserves company.

Rowan: Hm. Maybe you are learning.

=> END

~ friend_6
Rowan: I left a spare key for the workshop shelf. Do not make me regret that sentence.
- That almost sounds like trust.
	Rowan: Do not ruin it by naming it.
	=> END

~ friend_8
Rowan: The bridge sounds different after a proper repair. Less complaining in the joints.
- You can hear that?
	Rowan: You can too. You just have to stop talking first.
	=> END

~ friend_10
Rowan: If I ever rebuild the whole waterwheel, I already know who I am asking to stand on the unsafe side.
- That is your highest compliment yet.
	Rowan: Correct.
	=> END

~ heart_4
Rowan: Workshop fund came through. New braces, dry storage, tools that are not older than I am.
Rowan: Most people like finished buildings. You helped before there was anything impressive to look at.
- Foundations matter.
	Rowan: Now you are stealing my lines.
	=> END

~ heart_6
Rowan: Here. Take this plane for a moment.
Rowan: I do not lend that one out. The balance is right and replacing it would annoy me for years.
- Then why hand it to me?
	Rowan: Because I know you will hand it back in the same condition.
	=> END

~ heart_8
Rowan: I used to repair the bridge because somebody had to.
Rowan: Lately I catch myself thinking about what it connects instead of what might fail next.
- That sounds healthier.
	Rowan: Do not get ambitious. I still inspect every joint.
	=> END

~ heart_10
Rowan: Good structures are not one beam holding everything up. They work because the load gets shared.
Rowan: The towns finally feel like that again.
- And us?
	Rowan: Same principle. Reliable, tested, and worth maintaining.
	=> END
